# Fuzz delta, the last layer of `.env -> .env.dev -> .env.fuzz` (the harness sets
# ENV_FILES=".env.dev:.env.fuzz"). It carries ONLY the keys whose values differ
# from the layers beneath it; the Postgres-cluster block, DATABASE_PASSWORD,
# APP_DOMAIN, and the required-toggle dev values (e.g. GOOGLE_AUTH_PROVIDER=stub)
# are inherited from .env.dev.

# bin/test-fuzz derives this checkout's 16-port block with bin/checkout-port and
# exports its base as BASE_TEST_PORT, so a foreign listener on the dev ports
# (e.g. a running dev server) never blocks a fuzz run, and a fuzz run never
# lands inside another checkout's block. Deriving the ports here — rather than
# pinning them — is what makes the override survive: bin/common re-sources this
# delta in every child (rest-server-up, daemon-up, …), and a plain PORT= would
# reset each child back to `.env`'s default, clobbering the parent's export.
# BASE_TEST_PORT is read straight from the environment, so the derived block
# flows through unchanged. The offsets are the FUZZ half of the registry
# bin/checkout-port's help text carries: +7 rest-server, +8 admin-web, +9
# public-web — disjoint from the test half (+0..+6), so one checkout may run the
# test and fuzz suites at the same time (they use different databases).
# Unset (an ordinary non-fuzz run that somehow selected this file) falls back to
# the same 18080 base .env.test uses, well clear of the dev ports; the previous
# fallback landed on 8082, which is the dev PUBLIC_WEB_PORT (RFC 132).
#
# The base is repeated in each expression rather than held in a scratch variable
# on purpose: these files are sourced under `set -a`, so a helper assignment
# would be EXPORTED into every child's environment.
PORT=$(( ${BASE_TEST_PORT:-18080} + 7 ))
ADMIN_WEB_PORT=$(( ${BASE_TEST_PORT:-18080} + 8 ))
PUBLIC_WEB_PORT=$(( ${BASE_TEST_PORT:-18080} + 9 ))

# Per-worktree fuzz DB so concurrent fuzz runs across worktrees never collide.
# PROJECT_ROOT is set by bin/common before this file is sourced; the value is
# exported and flows to the JVM via db.conf's ${POSTGRES_DB}.
POSTGRES_DB=unicoach-fuzz-$(basename "$PROJECT_ROOT")

# --- Application Configuration (deltas vs .env) ---
DATABASE_USER=postgres
DATABASE_MAXIMUM_POOL_SIZE=2
# Re-derived after PORT.
SERVER_PORT=$PORT
